WEBVTT

00:00:30.427 --> 00:00:34.056
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:46.902
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION
SOME SCENES WERE GENERATED USING AI

00:00:46.985 --> 00:00:49.071
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

00:01:01.124 --> 00:01:03.126
[♪ melancholy music playing]

00:01:06.088 --> 00:01:12.469
I'm going to think of Seonu
every time I see you now.

00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:16.098
It's going to
be like this forever, isn't it?

00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:03.937
[chattering]

00:02:06.648 --> 00:02:08.859
[machine beeping]

00:02:13.196 --> 00:02:15.282
[breathes heavily]

00:02:19.745 --> 00:02:21.037
Dr. Do, are you okay?

00:02:22.873 --> 00:02:25.083
The patient's regained consciousness!

00:02:27.836 --> 00:02:29.045
[whispering] I'm okay.

00:02:29.963 --> 00:02:34.551
[announcer on PA speaks Korean]

00:02:39.389 --> 00:02:40.515
Deokhwa…

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.059
What about Deokhwa?

00:02:44.102 --> 00:02:45.896
[doctor] It's acute epiglottitis.

00:02:45.979 --> 00:02:48.482
She's currently unresponsive
under sedation,

00:02:48.565 --> 00:02:50.692
but depending on
her condition or progress,

00:02:50.776 --> 00:02:53.445
we'll taper the dosage
to help her regain consciousness.

00:02:54.696 --> 00:02:57.199
With acute epiglottitis,
we need to put her on antibiotics

00:02:57.282 --> 00:02:58.784
and monitor her closely.

00:02:58.867 --> 00:03:03.538
The concern is that potential
complications could lead to brain damage,

00:03:03.622 --> 00:03:05.290
or in severe cases, even death.

00:03:05.373 --> 00:03:09.169
[crying] No!

00:03:09.252 --> 00:03:11.296
Oh, Deokhwa!

00:03:12.756 --> 00:03:16.802
Doctor, please save Deokhwa.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.598
My dear girl…

00:03:21.681 --> 00:03:23.934
What the doctor just said

00:03:24.851 --> 00:03:29.648
was the absolute worst-case scenario
that could happen.

00:03:31.233 --> 00:03:34.861
We caught it early
and treated her right away.

00:03:34.945 --> 00:03:38.406
And it's rare for a child
to suffer permanent brain damage,

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.367
so you don't need to worry too much.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.704
But earlier on, the doctor said Deokhwa…

00:03:44.788 --> 00:03:47.499
That's just what a doctor has to do.

00:03:49.543 --> 00:03:55.715
Doctors have to be prepared
for the absolute worst-case scenarios,

00:03:56.758 --> 00:03:59.844
just to ensure the patient gets
the best possible care.

00:04:00.595 --> 00:04:02.681
[parent sniffles]

00:04:06.726 --> 00:04:08.728
You should also get treated, ma'am.

00:04:09.563 --> 00:04:10.689
Sorry? [sniffs]

00:04:10.772 --> 00:04:12.649
I'm talking about your feet.

00:04:14.401 --> 00:04:16.486
Oh, I'm perfectly fine.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.196
I'm okay.

00:04:18.863 --> 00:04:21.533
But something horrible
could have happened to you earlier
STYLE
::cue()

00:04:21.616 --> 00:04:23.076
because of us, though.

00:04:23.159 --> 00:04:24.327
I'm so sorry.

00:04:25.245 --> 00:04:28.123
-I'm really sorry.
-[chuckles]

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.335
It's okay. I just passed out for a moment.

00:04:33.253 --> 00:04:34.254
I'm fine.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:41.511
-But…
-[stammering] Oh, I'm completely fine.

00:04:41.595 --> 00:04:43.221
I'm totally okay. [chuckles]

00:04:43.305 --> 00:04:46.850
[parent]
But you also fell in the water too.

00:04:46.933 --> 00:04:48.226
[Hari] I'm fine.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.978
[parent] Are you really okay?

00:04:56.818 --> 00:04:58.820
[♪ surreal music playing]

00:05:30.018 --> 00:05:36.608
EPISODE 5
PYEONDONG SCANDAL

00:05:39.361 --> 00:05:40.362
Dr. Do.

00:05:42.113 --> 00:05:43.114
-Yes?
-[parent sniffles]

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:45.575
Oh. [chuckles]

00:05:45.659 --> 00:05:46.826
[parent cries]

00:05:47.661 --> 00:05:48.662
Oh.

00:05:50.622 --> 00:05:53.458
[elevator bell dinging]

00:05:53.541 --> 00:05:54.626
[doors opening]

00:05:55.669 --> 00:05:59.005
-[announcer speaks indistinctly on PA]
-Why'd you do it? It was dangerous.

00:06:00.048 --> 00:06:02.050
It was nothing.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:03.510
I'm a great swimmer.

00:06:04.427 --> 00:06:07.263
I may not look it,
but I was born and raised on an island.

00:06:15.313 --> 00:06:19.359
-But still--
-Jeez, what are you hesitating for?

00:06:20.652 --> 00:06:22.696
Just thank me and be done with it.

00:06:25.323 --> 00:06:28.868
We both made it out okay,
so that's all that matters.

00:06:32.288 --> 00:06:33.999
Thank you.

00:06:34.082 --> 00:06:36.960
[♪ soft music playing]

00:06:37.043 --> 00:06:39.129
[automated voice] Basement One.

00:06:46.511 --> 00:06:48.221
I also want to thank you.

00:06:50.849 --> 00:06:52.475
You saved them both.

00:06:54.018 --> 00:06:55.979
Deokhwa and her mom.

00:06:58.231 --> 00:06:59.983
[doors closing]

00:07:02.694 --> 00:07:03.987
[staff] Please make way.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.780
-Coming through.
-[staff] Thank you.

00:07:11.327 --> 00:07:12.912
[automated voice] The doors are closing.

00:07:27.302 --> 00:07:28.762
[automated voice] First floor.

00:07:34.768 --> 00:07:37.187
Hmm? Ms. Yuk Hari?

00:07:38.104 --> 00:07:39.105
[gasps]

00:07:39.773 --> 00:07:41.524
So it was you, Ms. Yuk Hari!

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:45.570
The nurses said
they ran into you in the ER,

00:07:45.653 --> 00:07:47.322
and I told them there was no way.

00:07:47.405 --> 00:07:49.073
But it is you!

00:07:49.908 --> 00:07:52.160
Yes, well, it's a long story…

00:07:52.243 --> 00:07:54.537
[nurse] You should have let us know
if you were coming.

00:07:56.664 --> 00:07:59.959
But who's this next to you?

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.129
Ah, he's a doctor I work with.

00:08:03.213 --> 00:08:04.214
[nurse] Oh.

00:08:04.297 --> 00:08:07.175
A doctor you work with, huh?

00:08:08.009 --> 00:08:11.805
Hello, I'm a nurse who used to
work with Ms. Yuk.

00:08:11.888 --> 00:08:13.598
Yes. I'm Do Jiui.

00:08:13.681 --> 00:08:16.476
We should get going now.
He's still a patient, so…

00:08:16.559 --> 00:08:18.228
Let's go.

00:08:24.359 --> 00:08:26.361
[♪ comical music playing]

00:08:32.826 --> 00:08:36.538
[nurse] Yuk Hari came to the hospital.
With a guy.
STYLE
::cue()

00:08:38.748 --> 00:08:41.125
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

00:08:41.209 --> 00:08:43.127
[phone ringing]

00:08:43.837 --> 00:08:45.171
Ms. Yuk?

00:08:45.255 --> 00:08:47.382
[Hari] Yes. I made you worry, didn't I?

00:08:48.007 --> 00:08:51.636
Deokhwa's being treated with antibiotics,
and Dr. Do is also okay.

00:08:51.719 --> 00:08:52.720
What about you?

00:08:52.804 --> 00:08:54.264
[chuckles]

00:08:54.347 --> 00:08:56.516
-I'm also doing okay.
-[sighs]

00:08:56.599 --> 00:08:57.767
What did she say?

00:08:58.434 --> 00:09:01.437
We'll return as soon as
we get Dr. Do's results.

00:09:01.521 --> 00:09:03.523
Okay. I'll let everyone know.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.072
She said everyone's okay.

00:09:12.198 --> 00:09:13.575
[sighs]

00:09:13.658 --> 00:09:16.161
-[Ms. Hwang] Oh, what a relief.
-[breathes heavily]

00:09:16.244 --> 00:09:19.789
We didn't hear back for so long,
I was afraid something happened to them.

00:09:19.873 --> 00:09:22.250
I know, right? Me too.

00:09:22.333 --> 00:09:25.461
Since she said everyone's all right,
let's all get back to work.

00:09:25.545 --> 00:09:29.465
We're down two people today,
so let's get it together.

00:09:29.549 --> 00:09:30.550
Okay.

00:09:32.302 --> 00:09:33.511
[sighs]

00:09:47.859 --> 00:09:50.570
[inhales sharply] Isn't it really weird?

00:09:51.571 --> 00:09:53.781
He cares way too much about her.

00:09:53.865 --> 00:09:57.160
Yes. Really weird.

00:09:58.703 --> 00:10:02.373
Your test results are all clear,
but you do have a mild concussion.

00:10:02.457 --> 00:10:05.752
You should stay the night at the hospital
for further monitoring.

00:10:06.586 --> 00:10:07.587
Okay.

00:10:13.051 --> 00:10:14.594
[exhales]

00:10:18.389 --> 00:10:20.099
[stammers] Are you leaving?

00:10:20.725 --> 00:10:23.436
Oh, no, I was just heading out
to the convenience store.

00:10:24.604 --> 00:10:25.605
Oh.

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:31.527
Does it scare you a little
because you're here as a patient?

00:10:32.695 --> 00:10:33.821
[sighs]

00:10:33.905 --> 00:10:36.616
Just wait a little.
I'll be back before they give you a shot.

00:10:51.297 --> 00:10:53.758
[register beeping, whirring]

00:11:03.226 --> 00:11:05.061
[nurse 1] Did you hear?

00:11:05.144 --> 00:11:06.771
I heard Yuk Hari's here.

00:11:07.563 --> 00:11:10.400
She came in with that emergency patient
who fell overboard.

00:11:10.483 --> 00:11:13.695
Wow. To think she came here
knowing that Dr. Dongseop's here.

00:11:13.778 --> 00:11:17.240
-And with a guy. She's unbelievable.
-[nurse 1 chuckling]

00:11:17.323 --> 00:11:18.616
I know, right?

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:22.954
What's even crazier is that
the guy's apparently a PH doc.

00:11:23.913 --> 00:11:26.291
I guess the rumors are true.

00:11:26.374 --> 00:11:28.543
That Yuk Hari is a doctor hunter.

00:11:28.626 --> 00:11:29.627
[nurse 2] For sure.

00:11:29.711 --> 00:11:31.796
[nurses giggling]

00:11:40.054 --> 00:11:42.724
[nurse 1] Gosh, you have no idea.

00:11:42.807 --> 00:11:45.268
It was a huge scandal here back then.

00:11:45.351 --> 00:11:47.270
We all had to walk on eggshells…

00:11:53.818 --> 00:11:56.988
Feel free to let me know
if there's anything you'd like to know.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.283
I'll be going now.

00:12:07.206 --> 00:12:09.167
[nurses whispering]

00:12:15.048 --> 00:12:16.799
[objects clattering]

00:12:16.883 --> 00:12:21.220
[patient] What do you mean,
you can't do it? Huh?

00:12:21.304 --> 00:12:25.266
You're a doctor,
so do your job and treat me, okay?
STYLE
::cue()

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:26.851
What's going on?

00:12:26.934 --> 00:12:29.103
Talk some sense into him, would you?

00:12:29.187 --> 00:12:31.564
See this? I even took my shirt off,

00:12:31.647 --> 00:12:34.359
but he suddenly says he won't
give me acupuncture treatment.

00:12:35.109 --> 00:12:37.737
Don't you have a duty to treat a patient?

00:12:39.113 --> 00:12:41.324
Why won't you say anything?

00:12:41.407 --> 00:12:44.535
Say something, okay? Hey!

00:12:45.661 --> 00:12:48.247
-[Jeongseon] Please let go and--
-Are you looking down on me?

00:12:50.166 --> 00:12:52.210
-That's enough.
-What's this?

00:12:52.293 --> 00:12:55.046
Trust me, you don't want to do this to me.

00:12:55.129 --> 00:12:56.798
-[bones crack]
-[patient exclaims]

00:12:56.881 --> 00:12:59.634
Interfering with medical care
or assaulting healthcare workers

00:12:59.717 --> 00:13:00.718
is a serious crime.

00:13:00.802 --> 00:13:03.930
Hey, you're the one who's assaulting me!

00:13:04.013 --> 00:13:06.307
-Do you even know who I am? [strains]
-[bones cracking]

00:13:06.391 --> 00:13:08.059
[Hyeon] I have no idea who you are.

00:13:08.142 --> 00:13:10.144
Should I call the cops
so we can identify you?

00:13:10.228 --> 00:13:12.939
[stammering] Hey, I get it.

00:13:13.022 --> 00:13:15.358
Why call the cops all of a sudden?
Damn it.

00:13:15.441 --> 00:13:18.694
Let go, I get it. [grunting]

00:13:18.778 --> 00:13:21.447
Why you little… I work out, man.

00:13:22.073 --> 00:13:23.866
Call the cops. Call whoever you want.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.451
Screw that. You know what?

00:13:25.535 --> 00:13:30.790
You can even call those punks in the US,
the NFS, for all I care, damn it!

00:13:31.499 --> 00:13:34.669
-I'll kill every last one of them.
-Oh my, Mr. Yeom, what is it?

00:13:34.752 --> 00:13:37.380
-What?
-I'm busy, so I'm heading out now.

00:13:39.841 --> 00:13:41.801
[Ms. Hwang] What would
a bunch of young 'uns know?

00:13:41.884 --> 00:13:44.971
-[objects clatter]
-I'll give them a proper scolding.

00:13:45.054 --> 00:13:46.055
Oh, dear…

00:13:46.139 --> 00:13:48.933
[Hyeon] That prick doesn't even know
what the NFS is.

00:13:53.729 --> 00:13:58.442
[phone ringing]

00:13:59.443 --> 00:14:01.696
Hello, Mr. Ko, sir! Yes.

00:14:02.446 --> 00:14:06.534
The construction?
It's going very smoothly, sir.

00:14:07.243 --> 00:14:11.706
Don't you worry. Yes, of course.

00:14:12.331 --> 00:14:13.332
Two thousand won?

00:14:13.416 --> 00:14:15.960
I'll be sure to wrap things up
within the deadline.

00:14:17.753 --> 00:14:20.006
I understand, sir. You know me.

00:14:20.089 --> 00:14:21.716
I'm Yeom Byeongcheol.

00:14:21.799 --> 00:14:23.718
We've got plenty of time.

00:14:23.801 --> 00:14:26.637
Yes. I understand.
I pledge my undying loyalty to you, sir!

00:14:26.721 --> 00:14:29.432
Hey, isn't that Byeongcheol?

00:14:29.515 --> 00:14:31.434
When did he get here?

00:14:32.268 --> 00:14:36.147
I heard he's been put in charge
of the helipad construction project.

00:14:37.899 --> 00:14:39.984
He must've cozied up
to some mainland big shots.

00:14:40.067 --> 00:14:41.527
Helipad construction project?

00:14:42.153 --> 00:14:43.154
Goodness.

00:14:43.237 --> 00:14:46.115
Why are they tearing down
a perfectly functional helipad?

00:14:46.199 --> 00:14:48.659
That guy's going to stir up trouble again.

00:14:48.743 --> 00:14:50.453
This is driving me crazy.

00:15:17.355 --> 00:15:19.482
What's gotten into you?

00:15:22.235 --> 00:15:26.614
I was the one who examined Deokhwa first.

00:15:28.241 --> 00:15:30.409
If I had examined her properly…

00:15:32.286 --> 00:15:33.829
what happened to Deokhwa…

00:15:35.498 --> 00:15:36.999
Dr. Jiui…

00:15:38.876 --> 00:15:40.544
and Ms. Hari…

00:15:42.255 --> 00:15:43.256
[sniffs]

00:15:44.924 --> 00:15:47.510
…could have been prevented.
[breathes shakily]

00:15:56.269 --> 00:15:57.853
I'm scared…

00:15:59.939 --> 00:16:01.524
of treating my patients.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.570
[sniffs, breathes heavily]
STYLE
::cue()

00:16:25.715 --> 00:16:27.717
[♪ soft guitar music playing]

00:16:41.564 --> 00:16:42.648
Aren't you hungry?

00:16:44.191 --> 00:16:46.569
Well… A little.

00:16:46.652 --> 00:16:48.446
[Hari exclaims]

00:16:54.035 --> 00:16:56.245
-Let's dig in.
-Please, help yourself.

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:24.190
Do you like hamburgers?

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.069
Yes, I do.

00:17:28.861 --> 00:17:30.655
I love everything about our clinic,

00:17:30.738 --> 00:17:32.698
except that there are no burger places.

00:17:35.034 --> 00:17:37.370
You must really like hamburgers.

00:17:37.453 --> 00:17:39.622
Yes. It's my comfort food.

00:17:39.705 --> 00:17:41.123
[chuckles]

00:17:42.458 --> 00:17:43.626
Ever since I was little,

00:17:43.709 --> 00:17:47.505
my grandma bought me hamburgers
whenever something bad happened.

00:17:48.964 --> 00:17:52.093
When I got into a fight with a friend,
when I tanked an exam,

00:17:52.802 --> 00:17:54.804
and even when I was scolded by my grandma.

00:17:56.263 --> 00:17:58.641
You must be really close
with your grandmother.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:00.935
We're super close.

00:18:01.018 --> 00:18:02.019
[chuckles]

00:18:02.103 --> 00:18:05.189
Ever since I was little,
my grandma was all I had in the world.

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:11.570
My grandma's my mom, my dad, my friend,
and everything.

00:18:11.654 --> 00:18:12.780
She's my everything.

00:18:12.863 --> 00:18:13.989
[chuckles]

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:20.454
[exclaims]

00:18:20.538 --> 00:18:22.248
-You've got ketchup on you.
-[grunts]

00:18:25.668 --> 00:18:26.752
Um…

00:18:27.336 --> 00:18:28.587
-Thank you.
-[Hari] Right there.

00:18:28.671 --> 00:18:29.672
[Jiui grunts]

00:18:33.676 --> 00:18:36.554
[nurse 1] I guess the rumors are true.

00:18:36.637 --> 00:18:38.597
That Yuk Hari is a doctor hunter.

00:18:38.681 --> 00:18:40.683
[♪ soft music playing]

00:18:42.268 --> 00:18:45.312
Feel free to let me know
if there's anything you'd like to know.

00:18:54.363 --> 00:18:57.158
Hey, Dr. Do…

00:19:00.578 --> 00:19:01.871
Did you…

00:19:11.255 --> 00:19:12.256
Never mind.

00:19:18.053 --> 00:19:19.054
Um…

00:19:20.347 --> 00:19:22.433
I'm done eating, so I'll get going now.

00:19:24.518 --> 00:19:27.438
The ferries have probably
stopped running though.

00:19:27.521 --> 00:19:29.064
I'll just get a room.

00:19:34.528 --> 00:19:36.363
Let's meet at the port tomorrow.

00:19:40.075 --> 00:19:41.368
Ms. Yuk…
STYLE
::cue()

00:19:47.291 --> 00:19:49.293
[♪ melancholy music playing]

00:19:51.462 --> 00:19:52.505
[sighs]

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.676
[sighs]

00:20:12.191 --> 00:20:13.692
-Hari.
-[grunts]

00:20:13.776 --> 00:20:15.945
-[gasps]
-[panting]

00:20:16.028 --> 00:20:17.613
Why didn't you pick up your phone?

00:20:17.696 --> 00:20:19.073
I called you so many times.

00:20:19.865 --> 00:20:21.325
Do you know how worried I was?

00:20:28.582 --> 00:20:30.334
I heard you transferred to an island.

00:20:30.417 --> 00:20:31.585
How are things there?

00:20:31.669 --> 00:20:33.504
I'd been meaning to visit you, but…

00:20:38.634 --> 00:20:41.178
Looks like you've been doing well.
You look good.

00:20:42.346 --> 00:20:45.182
I haven't been doing so great.
I've been thinking about you a lot.

00:20:45.266 --> 00:20:47.184
Yeah, I could tell.

00:20:48.978 --> 00:20:50.980
They're still gossiping about me here.

00:20:52.356 --> 00:20:54.525
Apparently,
I'm a doctor-hunter gold digger.

00:20:54.608 --> 00:20:55.651
[exhales]

00:20:55.734 --> 00:20:59.113
Well, people are misunderstanding
because I'm struggling so--

00:20:59.196 --> 00:21:00.239
Misunderstanding?

00:21:01.615 --> 00:21:03.576
I assume that was your intention.

00:21:05.369 --> 00:21:07.663
I'm sure you made me the bad guy,

00:21:07.746 --> 00:21:09.456
so you can look like a good guy.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:10.541
Hari.

00:21:12.793 --> 00:21:14.336
Let's stop fighting now.

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:15.838
I told you I was sorry.

00:21:15.921 --> 00:21:18.340
We're not fighting. We broke up, okay?

00:21:18.424 --> 00:21:20.342
What do you mean, "we broke up"?

00:21:20.426 --> 00:21:22.386
I'm not breaking up with you!

00:21:24.471 --> 00:21:26.724
I told you I'm not breaking up with you.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.769
Why? Is it because of
that PH doc you came here with?

00:21:31.437 --> 00:21:32.980
Is that prick better than me? Huh?

00:21:34.773 --> 00:21:36.358
So you want to move on with him?

00:21:36.442 --> 00:21:39.069
Forget it. I have nothing to say to you.

00:21:39.153 --> 00:21:40.738
Where do you think you're going?
How dare you?

00:21:40.821 --> 00:21:42.406
I'm not done talking to you.

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:44.491
[Hari] Dr. Do!

00:21:45.951 --> 00:21:47.286
Who the hell are you?

00:21:49.038 --> 00:21:51.832
Oh, so you're the PH doc
she came here with?

00:21:52.583 --> 00:21:53.584
[grunts]

00:21:55.127 --> 00:21:57.713
-Dr. Do, let go.
-[Dongseop grunts]

00:21:57.796 --> 00:21:59.048
[Hari] Let's just go.

00:21:59.715 --> 00:22:01.383
There's nothing more to be said.

00:22:03.344 --> 00:22:04.845
You better snap out of it!

00:22:07.681 --> 00:22:10.100
She's not really into you.

00:22:10.768 --> 00:22:13.020
She's dated three doctors here,
including me!

00:22:14.104 --> 00:22:16.815
She jumps ship
the second someone better comes along.

00:22:18.233 --> 00:22:19.234
She's a gold digger.

00:22:21.028 --> 00:22:24.281
I'm saying she's got her hooks in you!

00:22:27.076 --> 00:22:29.870
I don't care
if she's a gold digger or not.

00:22:34.667 --> 00:22:37.127
I've been begging her
to get her hooks in me, actually.

00:22:37.962 --> 00:22:39.046
What?

00:22:44.927 --> 00:22:46.095
Sheesh.

00:22:51.308 --> 00:22:53.310
But honestly, it's a huge relief.

00:22:54.395 --> 00:22:57.231
Because anyone with eyes
can see who the better man is.

00:22:58.899 --> 00:23:01.568
So know your place and get lost, will you?

00:23:02.361 --> 00:23:04.321
You and I don't belong in the same league.

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:11.245
Let's go, Ms. Yuk.

00:23:19.044 --> 00:23:20.337
-What?
-[nurse 1] What was that?
STYLE
::cue()

00:23:20.421 --> 00:23:22.297
[nurse 2] Did he just get dumped?

00:23:23.632 --> 00:23:26.093
[nurse 3] Then it's his second time
getting dumped.

00:23:42.192 --> 00:23:43.736
[sighs, mutters]

00:23:46.405 --> 00:23:50.409
I'm sorry you had to get involved
in my messy affair.

00:23:51.452 --> 00:23:53.829
There's nothing messy about it.

00:23:53.912 --> 00:23:55.748
That's on them.

00:23:58.083 --> 00:24:01.295
Didn't you hear all about me
from Ms. Sujeong earlier on?

00:24:02.254 --> 00:24:04.339
No, I didn't hear a thing she said.

00:24:04.423 --> 00:24:06.925
It all sounded like useless drivel anyway.

00:24:10.971 --> 00:24:15.642
I dated people and broke up with them,
just like everyone else…

00:24:18.062 --> 00:24:20.397
but people called me
a doctor-hunter gold digger.

00:24:23.192 --> 00:24:27.863
I didn't take you for the type
to let such rumors get to you.

00:24:29.406 --> 00:24:31.658
I didn't think so myself.

00:24:34.703 --> 00:24:39.625
I thought I didn't care about
what people said behind my back,

00:24:40.584 --> 00:24:43.045
since they knew nothing about
who I really am.

00:24:43.128 --> 00:24:45.923
[♪ soft guitar music playing]

00:24:46.006 --> 00:24:48.175
But I guess I was just acting tough.

00:24:50.469 --> 00:24:53.764
Seeing you alone with Ms. Sujeong earlier…

00:24:55.474 --> 00:24:57.351
really scared me.

00:24:58.811 --> 00:25:02.314
I was worried you might also
start believing those rumors about me.

00:25:02.397 --> 00:25:03.649
[chuckles]

00:25:03.732 --> 00:25:06.985
And it felt like you were
keeping your distance from me, and…

00:25:08.112 --> 00:25:10.155
that just made me mad and scared.

00:25:12.366 --> 00:25:17.162
So about what happened earlier, I…

00:25:18.038 --> 00:25:21.750
I know. I was just paranoid
because my conscience got the best of me.

00:25:22.960 --> 00:25:24.211
[chuckles]

00:25:30.551 --> 00:25:33.595
I pretended I came
to Pyeondongdo for my grandma…

00:25:34.972 --> 00:25:38.267
But to be honest, I ran away so I could
find comfort in her embrace.

00:25:40.394 --> 00:25:42.104
Like a coward.

00:25:48.068 --> 00:25:49.820
Everyone runs…

00:25:51.655 --> 00:25:53.240
when the pain gets unbearable.

00:25:55.951 --> 00:25:57.744
I also run away a lot.

00:26:03.667 --> 00:26:05.043
Want me to buy you a burger?

00:26:05.127 --> 00:26:06.670
What?

00:26:06.753 --> 00:26:09.006
I actually know
a great burger joint nearby.

00:26:09.089 --> 00:26:12.551
[laughing]

00:26:12.634 --> 00:26:15.637
I know you didn't even finish
half your burger earlier.

00:26:15.721 --> 00:26:16.930
You're right.

00:26:26.523 --> 00:26:28.692
Get some rest. I'll be going now.

00:26:32.905 --> 00:26:35.073
-Are you going?
-Huh?

00:26:35.157 --> 00:26:38.452
I mean, what kind of nurse
just leaves a patient behind?

00:26:39.244 --> 00:26:42.956
I told you. This is my first time
being treated as a patient, so…

00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:44.249
I'm really scared.

00:26:44.333 --> 00:26:46.793
[♪ comical music playing]

00:26:47.669 --> 00:26:49.504
[both chuckle]
STYLE
::cue()

00:26:51.340 --> 00:26:52.883
Mother.

00:26:52.966 --> 00:26:54.092
[grandmother] Hello?

00:26:54.176 --> 00:26:55.969
Had anything to eat yet?

00:26:56.053 --> 00:26:58.972
[sobbing] Yes, Deokhwa already ate.

00:26:59.056 --> 00:27:02.893
I was asking about you, not Deokhwa.
Have you had anything to eat yet?

00:27:03.727 --> 00:27:06.396
[parent] I'm sorry, Mother.

00:27:06.480 --> 00:27:09.149
Goodness, stop crying.

00:27:09.233 --> 00:27:11.568
You saved Deokhwa's life.

00:27:12.277 --> 00:27:16.073
Be sure to eat well
and go straight to bed. Okay.

00:27:17.199 --> 00:27:19.243
Isn't it such a relief?

00:27:19.826 --> 00:27:22.913
-They all made it out alive.
-Gosh, I know.

00:27:22.996 --> 00:27:26.249
This is all thanks to you, Mr. Park.

00:27:26.333 --> 00:27:29.211
Come now, I can't take the credit.

00:27:29.294 --> 00:27:31.588
The real hero is Ms. Hari.

00:27:31.672 --> 00:27:34.633
She flung herself into
the pitch-black waters just like that.

00:27:34.716 --> 00:27:37.052
The more I think about it,
the more amazed I am.

00:27:37.135 --> 00:27:40.639
She dived right in
without a moment of hesitation.

00:27:41.431 --> 00:27:43.517
What's this about Hari
diving into the water?

00:27:44.184 --> 00:27:45.310
Mija, the thing is…

00:27:45.394 --> 00:27:47.896
Hey, what were you talking about just now?

00:27:47.980 --> 00:27:50.232
What do you mean,
Hari flung herself into the water?

00:27:50.315 --> 00:27:52.526
Well, you see--

00:27:52.609 --> 00:27:57.823
So, Hari wasn't simply
accompanying them to the hospital.

00:27:57.906 --> 00:28:00.409
She ended up going
because she fell into the sea?

00:28:00.492 --> 00:28:01.660
Mija, you see--

00:28:01.743 --> 00:28:06.498
I mean, how could no one
talk her out of doing something like that?

00:28:06.581 --> 00:28:08.959
[Mr. Park] We had no time
to talk her out of it.

00:28:09.042 --> 00:28:12.295
She dived in to save Dr. Do
the moment he went overboard.

00:28:12.379 --> 00:28:14.923
You still should have
talked her out of it!

00:28:15.007 --> 00:28:16.258
My goodness.

00:28:16.341 --> 00:28:19.553
What was she thinking,
jumping into the sea like that?

00:28:19.636 --> 00:28:22.556
Hari, what were you thinking? [gasps]

00:28:23.181 --> 00:28:25.851
[grunting]

00:28:25.934 --> 00:28:27.019
[groans]

00:28:28.937 --> 00:28:30.022
-[grunts]
-Huh?

00:28:30.647 --> 00:28:31.857
[Mija groans]

00:28:32.899 --> 00:28:35.235
-Are you okay, ma'am?
-[panting]

00:28:38.947 --> 00:28:39.948
[Hyeon] It's a painkiller.

00:28:40.741 --> 00:28:42.701
I'm sure the stress caused the migraines.

00:28:48.498 --> 00:28:49.666
[sighs]

00:28:50.500 --> 00:28:51.501
[sniffs]

00:28:52.836 --> 00:28:57.632
I'll have you know I'm not particularly
fond of the public health center, either.

00:28:57.716 --> 00:29:03.513
You've got young doctors and two nurses
other than Hari, but of all people,

00:29:04.139 --> 00:29:09.352
you sent my precious granddaughter
in the middle of the night…

00:29:09.436 --> 00:29:10.729
I'm sorry, ma'am.

00:29:14.107 --> 00:29:19.362
And while we're on the subject,
let me ask you something else.

00:29:20.322 --> 00:29:23.992
Do you like Hari?

00:29:24.993 --> 00:29:25.994
[chuckles]

00:29:26.078 --> 00:29:32.334
I know what the villagers have been saying
about you and Hari.

00:29:32.417 --> 00:29:35.337
That's another thing
that really bothers me,

00:29:36.254 --> 00:29:40.801
so please stop sending her false signals
by pretending that you care about her.

00:29:43.720 --> 00:29:45.806
I wasn't pretending.

00:29:47.933 --> 00:29:48.934
What now?

00:29:54.356 --> 00:29:55.732
You sleep here, Ms. Yuk.

00:29:55.816 --> 00:29:58.443
[stammers] No way.
You're the patient here.

00:29:58.527 --> 00:30:01.363
So listen to the patient.
Do you want to stress out the patient?

00:30:01.446 --> 00:30:04.116
-Absolutely not. Hurry up and lie down.
-[patient] For goodness' sake.

00:30:04.199 --> 00:30:05.534
Keep it down, will you?

00:30:06.118 --> 00:30:08.537
See that? Are you seriously
going to stress out your patient?

00:30:08.620 --> 00:30:11.498
-Hurry up and lie down.
-[stammers]

00:30:11.581 --> 00:30:12.582
Seriously…

00:30:12.666 --> 00:30:14.584
[Jiui grunting]

00:30:14.668 --> 00:30:17.420
Whatever. I'm already lying down.

00:30:18.213 --> 00:30:19.381
[Hari sighs]

00:30:21.091 --> 00:30:22.592
[whispering] See? It's too small for you.

00:30:22.676 --> 00:30:24.886
-You'll be uncomfortable.
-[whispering] I'll be fine.

00:30:27.222 --> 00:30:28.849
-Seriously…
-[Jiui chuckles]

00:30:42.070 --> 00:30:43.071
Ms. Hari.

00:30:43.822 --> 00:30:44.823
Yes?

00:30:48.577 --> 00:30:49.953
Earlier on…

00:30:50.704 --> 00:30:54.499
[patient coughs, clearing throat]

00:30:58.879 --> 00:31:00.088
Never mind.

00:31:00.172 --> 00:31:01.381
Good night.

00:31:16.813 --> 00:31:20.901
A BEAUTIFUL YEOPOONG,
HAPPY RESIDENTS

00:31:21.902 --> 00:31:24.112
[Changmok] Crap, I didn't cut it straight.

00:31:25.655 --> 00:31:28.617
You handled the Pyeondongdo matter
as I said, right?
STYLE
::cue()

00:31:30.035 --> 00:31:32.662
I'm afraid taking disciplinary action
against the PH doc

00:31:32.746 --> 00:31:35.373
isn't really an option.

00:31:37.417 --> 00:31:39.836
What nonsense is this now?

00:31:39.920 --> 00:31:43.256
There was an incident
on the day I arrived.

00:31:43.340 --> 00:31:46.176
There was a medical emergency
involving a child,

00:31:46.259 --> 00:31:48.720
but the PH doc
who was due to receive the warning,

00:31:48.803 --> 00:31:51.056
risked his life to save her.

00:31:51.139 --> 00:31:53.099
Issuing a warning to a doctor like that

00:31:53.183 --> 00:31:55.894
would have had a negative impact
on their morale, so--

00:31:55.977 --> 00:31:59.272
Hold on, so you're saying
the Pyeondongdo PH doc

00:31:59.356 --> 00:32:02.359
risked his life to save a child's life?

00:32:02.442 --> 00:32:03.443
Yes.

00:32:04.236 --> 00:32:08.657
Well, in that case,
I'll have to meet up with that PH doc.

00:32:09.241 --> 00:32:10.242
What?

00:32:10.325 --> 00:32:11.368
Don't you get it?

00:32:11.451 --> 00:32:14.246
That's exactly
the kind of story I could use

00:32:14.329 --> 00:32:16.623
as someone who dreams
of modernizing health care.

00:32:16.706 --> 00:32:18.041
Try to keep up.

00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:20.502
[inhales sharply]

00:32:20.585 --> 00:32:22.796
Yes. I should meet him.

00:32:22.879 --> 00:32:24.339
ASONG UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

00:32:24.422 --> 00:32:26.591
[employee]
Here's your prescription and receipt.

00:32:27.467 --> 00:32:28.593
[Hari] Should we go now?

00:32:28.677 --> 00:32:29.678
Sure.

00:32:34.349 --> 00:32:35.892
The ferry's about to leave, so…

00:32:39.729 --> 00:32:41.273
I guess you're on your way now.

00:32:42.524 --> 00:32:43.608
Yes.

00:32:44.776 --> 00:32:48.947
You must've really settled in
on the island, Ms. Hari.

00:32:49.906 --> 00:32:51.700
Seeing you thrive like this
is such a relief.

00:32:52.534 --> 00:32:53.785
It really is a relief.

00:32:56.413 --> 00:32:57.414
Ms. Sujeong.

00:33:01.376 --> 00:33:03.378
I want you to know that I liked you all.

00:33:05.338 --> 00:33:08.008
I wanted to get along with everyone,

00:33:08.091 --> 00:33:11.553
and I wanted to work harder
to make you like me

00:33:11.636 --> 00:33:14.264
and to dispel all those weird rumors.

00:33:14.347 --> 00:33:16.891
But things didn't work out,
and that really bothered me.

00:33:19.185 --> 00:33:21.479
But leaving made me realize something.

00:33:26.192 --> 00:33:28.653
"I'm glad I left this dump."

00:33:29.237 --> 00:33:30.572
[both scoff]

00:33:30.655 --> 00:33:32.073
Ms. Yuk Hari!

00:33:32.157 --> 00:33:33.450
And one more thing.

00:33:37.746 --> 00:33:41.333
If you mess with me again,
I'm seriously going to kill you.

00:33:43.710 --> 00:33:44.711
Let's go.

00:33:44.794 --> 00:33:46.129
Oh, okay.

00:33:46.212 --> 00:33:47.213
[nurse scoffs]

00:33:51.801 --> 00:33:52.802
[gasps]

00:33:55.847 --> 00:33:58.099
[Ms. Hwang] What's this? Oh, goodness.

00:33:58.183 --> 00:33:59.517
[gasps]

00:33:59.601 --> 00:34:01.686
We'll be feasting on this until next year.

00:34:02.228 --> 00:34:04.522
-[chuckles]
-What's all this?

00:34:04.606 --> 00:34:08.485
I don't know how the villagers found out
Dr. Do was getting discharged,

00:34:08.568 --> 00:34:10.820
but it's been crazy since this morning.

00:34:11.696 --> 00:34:15.075
They brought in every healthy food
imaginable from land, sea, and air.

00:34:15.158 --> 00:34:17.035
We could throw a whole feast.

00:34:17.118 --> 00:34:21.247
But why is everyone
only looking for Dr. Do?

00:34:21.331 --> 00:34:23.583
There's someone else who needs to recover.

00:34:23.666 --> 00:34:25.794
-Huh?
-It's nothing.

00:34:25.877 --> 00:34:28.046
-I'll move all these.
-Put them in the fridge.

00:34:28.922 --> 00:34:30.590
[grunts, exclaims]

00:34:30.673 --> 00:34:33.385
[gasps] Oh, what happened?

00:34:33.468 --> 00:34:36.012
Ms. Eom! Jeongseon, where does it hurt?

00:34:36.596 --> 00:34:39.891
[Jeongseon winces] That hurts…

00:34:39.974 --> 00:34:42.060
That spot doesn't hurt.

00:34:42.143 --> 00:34:43.186
How does it look?

00:34:43.728 --> 00:34:44.896
[Hyeon] Hmm…

00:34:45.939 --> 00:34:47.649
It looks like you sprained your ankle.

00:34:47.732 --> 00:34:49.317
I'll prescribe some Enstaid for you.

00:34:49.401 --> 00:34:51.444
-That's not an option.
-Huh?

00:34:51.528 --> 00:34:54.155
I get side effects when I take steroids.

00:34:54.239 --> 00:34:56.783
Then you should get it treated
at the Korean Medicine Ward.

00:34:58.702 --> 00:35:00.662
The Korean Medicine Ward?

00:35:05.208 --> 00:35:06.751
Um, me?

00:35:08.753 --> 00:35:12.465
I think getting it treated on the mainland
might be the better option.

00:35:12.549 --> 00:35:13.800
Why's that?

00:35:15.218 --> 00:35:18.012
It looks like minor inflammation now,

00:35:18.096 --> 00:35:22.517
but it could be something more serious,
even a fracture.

00:35:22.600 --> 00:35:25.812
You should go to a hospital
on the mainland to get a proper diagnosis…

00:35:25.895 --> 00:35:27.439
Why would I do that?

00:35:27.522 --> 00:35:29.274
I have a doctor of Korean Medicine here,

00:35:29.357 --> 00:35:32.444
so why would I spend money
and time to go to the mainland?

00:35:32.527 --> 00:35:34.779
I'm just going to get it treated here.

00:35:34.863 --> 00:35:37.365
-Ms. Eom.
-What?

00:35:38.283 --> 00:35:39.868
Are you too scared to treat it?

00:35:44.164 --> 00:35:47.083
Then just leave it be.
I'll just try toughing it out.

00:35:48.001 --> 00:35:50.086
You really shouldn't be moving around--

00:35:50.170 --> 00:35:52.547
I guess I'll just drag my foot around.

00:36:03.308 --> 00:36:04.976
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

00:36:06.019 --> 00:36:11.149
[announcer] The ship bound for
Pyeondongdo, Pyeondongdo is now departing.

00:36:11.232 --> 00:36:13.985
Are you really going to be okay?

00:36:19.407 --> 00:36:21.951
[sighs] No.

00:36:22.035 --> 00:36:24.579
If you need your meds,
we can go back to the hospital to--

00:36:24.662 --> 00:36:27.415
But you said we should give this a go.

00:36:28.666 --> 00:36:30.710
While holding your hand.

00:36:31.461 --> 00:36:32.462
Uh…

00:36:33.797 --> 00:36:37.675
[ship horn blows]

00:36:40.845 --> 00:36:44.182
If I get too scared,
I'll just hold your hand.

00:36:44.891 --> 00:36:45.892
Hmm.

00:36:50.730 --> 00:36:51.731
Shall we go?

00:36:51.815 --> 00:36:53.316
[Hari whimpers]

00:37:12.502 --> 00:37:14.295
If you're so worried about me…

00:37:15.588 --> 00:37:18.424
That thing you played…
Let me listen to it again.

00:37:19.843 --> 00:37:20.844
What do you mean?

00:37:22.011 --> 00:37:23.888
The song you played for me back then.

00:37:25.098 --> 00:37:28.560
When you said music helps treat anxiety.

00:37:31.521 --> 00:37:33.523
I couldn't find it
no matter how hard I looked.

00:37:34.566 --> 00:37:36.067
You actually looked it up?

00:37:36.150 --> 00:37:39.654
I just figured it might be
some special music or something…

00:37:39.737 --> 00:37:42.615
[groans] And to think you were being
so difficult with me back then.

00:37:42.699 --> 00:37:44.033
Give me a second.

00:37:54.294 --> 00:37:56.296
[seagulls squawking]

00:37:58.298 --> 00:38:00.216
[♪ "This is How Love Begins" playing]

00:39:05.657 --> 00:39:09.661
YEOPOONG MARINE TRANSPORT

00:39:09.744 --> 00:39:12.163
[song continues]

00:39:36.104 --> 00:39:37.355
[song ends]

00:39:42.235 --> 00:39:43.319
[Jeongseon grunts]

00:39:43.403 --> 00:39:44.404
[exclaims]

00:39:45.905 --> 00:39:47.949
I must be getting old.

00:39:48.032 --> 00:39:49.575
My skin keeps breaking out.

00:39:55.164 --> 00:39:56.791
[Jucheon] It's so swollen.

00:39:58.251 --> 00:40:00.962
Ms. Eom, please stop being so stubborn

00:40:01.045 --> 00:40:03.381
and hurry over to a hospital, okay?

00:40:05.633 --> 00:40:06.718
I'm not going.

00:40:07.635 --> 00:40:10.930
If you leave the inflammation untreated,
it could become chronic.

00:40:11.014 --> 00:40:13.099
Something you'll deal with all your life.

00:40:13.182 --> 00:40:16.519
Which is why you can just patch me up.

00:40:17.353 --> 00:40:19.731
What the heck is the matter with you?

00:40:19.814 --> 00:40:21.899
I told you I'm scared, didn't I?

00:40:21.983 --> 00:40:23.985
If I were to mistreat someone--

00:40:24.068 --> 00:40:25.278
[Jeongseon] Goodness, Dr. Yong.

00:40:26.279 --> 00:40:28.906
You know you're beating yourself up
for no reason, right?

00:40:30.992 --> 00:40:31.993
What?

00:40:32.952 --> 00:40:37.081
Deokhwa was diagnosed
with acute epiglottitis.

00:40:37.165 --> 00:40:38.291
Not even Heo Jun…

00:40:38.374 --> 00:40:42.962
I mean, not even the greatest doctor
in history could have seen that coming.

00:40:43.046 --> 00:40:44.047
But still…

00:40:44.130 --> 00:40:47.300
What are you even doing here
if you're not going to do anything?

00:40:47.884 --> 00:40:50.803
If you're going to whine and ignore people
over one misdiagnosis,

00:40:50.887 --> 00:40:53.723
what's the point of you being here?
STYLE
::cue()

00:40:54.390 --> 00:40:57.310
Nobody's asking you to play God
and perform miracles, okay?

00:40:57.393 --> 00:41:00.188
Stop overthinking and just do your job.
[clicks tongue]

00:41:00.730 --> 00:41:04.317
So just hurry up and do something
about my leg. It's killing me!

00:41:15.620 --> 00:41:16.788
Hurry.

00:41:16.871 --> 00:41:19.248
It's not like I have any medicine to take.

00:41:24.128 --> 00:41:26.631
You're doing this
because you feel bad for me, right?

00:41:26.714 --> 00:41:29.008
What's this nonsense now?

00:41:29.092 --> 00:41:30.343
[clicks tongue]

00:41:32.095 --> 00:41:33.554
[sighs]

00:41:33.638 --> 00:41:36.307
I know you don't have side effects
from steroids.

00:41:37.350 --> 00:41:39.477
That medicine you applied earlier…

00:41:40.853 --> 00:41:42.313
It was a corticosteroid.

00:41:43.481 --> 00:41:45.608
[♪ soft music playing]

00:41:45.691 --> 00:41:46.859
[Jeongseon] Hmm.

00:41:48.277 --> 00:41:49.779
But I'll still give it a shot,

00:41:51.072 --> 00:41:52.532
since you trusted me.

00:41:53.616 --> 00:41:54.826
Please do.

00:41:56.202 --> 00:41:58.788
And hurry because I really am
in a lot of pain.

00:42:02.625 --> 00:42:04.293
[Jucheon sighs]

00:42:30.987 --> 00:42:32.280
Just a moment.

00:42:45.293 --> 00:42:47.461
-[Jeongseon] Cheers.
-[Jucheon] Cheers.

00:42:52.800 --> 00:42:54.051
[groans]

00:42:55.303 --> 00:42:57.180
-The thing about me is…
-Hmm.

00:42:58.347 --> 00:43:01.559
…I'm actually not a talkative person.

00:43:02.351 --> 00:43:04.187
-You?
-Yeah.

00:43:06.147 --> 00:43:09.775
I became talkative because I wanted people

00:43:10.443 --> 00:43:13.362
to like me so badly,

00:43:14.030 --> 00:43:16.282
and now I can't keep my mouth shut.

00:43:17.366 --> 00:43:19.076
[Jeongseon groaning]

00:43:19.160 --> 00:43:21.621
That's so sad.

00:43:21.704 --> 00:43:22.788
-[groans]
-Hmm.

00:43:22.872 --> 00:43:23.873
Isn't it?

00:43:25.333 --> 00:43:30.379
So I'm asking you to look out for me.

00:43:32.465 --> 00:43:34.425
Hmm. Okay!

00:43:34.967 --> 00:43:35.968
[grunts]

00:43:45.645 --> 00:43:47.230
[Jucheon] Hmm.

00:43:47.313 --> 00:43:51.275
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:43:52.151 --> 00:43:55.071
You just asked me to look out for you.

00:44:24.600 --> 00:44:26.727
-[Jucheon] All done, Ms. Eom.
-Huh?

00:44:26.811 --> 00:44:29.021
-Why don't you try getting up slowly?
-[groans]

00:44:35.653 --> 00:44:37.488
How is it? Feeling better now, right?

00:44:38.656 --> 00:44:41.575
Look how good you are at this.
All that whining for nothing.

00:44:46.956 --> 00:44:48.332
[groans]

00:44:48.416 --> 00:44:49.500
Thank you.

00:44:49.583 --> 00:44:50.710
Oh, Ms. Eom.

00:44:53.587 --> 00:44:54.588
Yes?

00:44:55.423 --> 00:44:57.591
Keep Mondays, Wednesdays,
and Fridays open for me.

00:44:59.051 --> 00:45:00.052
Huh?

00:45:00.136 --> 00:45:02.138
[♪ romantic music playing]

00:45:02.972 --> 00:45:04.849
For your acupuncture treatment.

00:45:08.519 --> 00:45:09.729
Fine by me.

00:45:24.076 --> 00:45:26.078
[breathes heavily]

00:45:26.162 --> 00:45:28.581
Why the hell is my heart beating so fast?

00:45:28.664 --> 00:45:30.166
I thought for sure he'd hear it.
STYLE
::cue()

00:45:38.507 --> 00:45:42.636
[ship horn blows]

00:45:48.768 --> 00:45:49.935
Huh?

00:45:53.147 --> 00:45:54.440
Huh?

00:45:54.523 --> 00:45:56.609
[panting]

00:45:56.692 --> 00:45:59.111
Dr. Do. Dr. Do, uh…

00:46:03.449 --> 00:46:05.284
[breathes heavily]

00:46:19.048 --> 00:46:20.091
[Hari gasps]

00:46:29.433 --> 00:46:30.726
[breathes heavily]

00:46:31.560 --> 00:46:33.562
[♪ soft music playing]

00:46:35.940 --> 00:46:37.608
[breathes heavily]

00:46:39.944 --> 00:46:41.195
[groans]

00:47:08.722 --> 00:47:10.266
[Hari] Let's go to the quarters together.

00:47:10.349 --> 00:47:11.350
I'll take you there.

00:47:12.309 --> 00:47:13.394
Oh, no, it's fine.

00:47:13.477 --> 00:47:15.771
Let me come with you. I'm just worried.

00:47:15.855 --> 00:47:17.648
I'm really feeling better now.

00:47:21.402 --> 00:47:22.653
[exhales]

00:47:26.115 --> 00:47:27.324
[Hari] Huh?

00:47:27.908 --> 00:47:29.618
Uh, Grandma!

00:47:30.119 --> 00:47:32.079
What are you doing out here, huh?

00:47:32.163 --> 00:47:33.205
Come with me.

00:47:34.707 --> 00:47:36.250
[Hari] What is it? Is something wrong?

00:47:36.333 --> 00:47:38.085
I said, come with me!

00:47:39.378 --> 00:47:40.921
I'm sorry, ma'am.

00:47:45.968 --> 00:47:49.013
I put Ms. Yuk in danger.

00:47:50.639 --> 00:47:52.766
I'm sorry to make you worry like that.

00:47:56.979 --> 00:48:01.358
I don't give a damn if you fall
into the ocean, or if you live or die.

00:48:01.442 --> 00:48:03.235
It's got nothing to do with me.

00:48:03.777 --> 00:48:09.408
I'm just terrified that Hari is going to
throw herself into danger again.

00:48:10.618 --> 00:48:13.579
Grandma, it wasn't because of Dr. Do.

00:48:13.662 --> 00:48:14.955
That was on me, okay?

00:48:15.873 --> 00:48:18.083
And besides,
it wasn't even that dangerous.

00:48:18.167 --> 00:48:22.296
Listen to yourself, you brat!

00:48:22.379 --> 00:48:23.464
[grunts]

00:48:23.547 --> 00:48:25.257
-Grandma!
-[Jiui] Oh, no!

00:48:26.008 --> 00:48:27.259
[Hari] Grandma!

00:48:27.343 --> 00:48:29.094
We should get her to the center.

00:48:29.178 --> 00:48:30.179
Right, okay.

00:48:31.263 --> 00:48:33.641
[Jiui panting]

00:48:33.724 --> 00:48:34.767
[grunts]

00:48:38.521 --> 00:48:40.356
PYEONDONGDO FISHERIES
COOPERATIVE
STYLE
::cue()

00:48:41.023 --> 00:48:42.691
What the… [grunts]

00:48:42.775 --> 00:48:43.776
Is that Mija?

00:48:44.360 --> 00:48:46.362
Goodness me, what happened?

00:48:49.532 --> 00:48:50.991
We have to get her to a hospital.

00:48:51.075 --> 00:48:53.661
It's a breast cancer patient
with possible brain metastasis.

00:48:53.744 --> 00:48:55.538
BREAST CANCER:
CANCER IN THE BREAST

00:48:55.621 --> 00:48:58.123
BRAIN METASTASIS:
CANCER SPREAD TO BRAIN

00:48:58.624 --> 00:48:59.833
[Hari] Grandma.

00:49:01.335 --> 00:49:03.754
-Hurry!
-[Jeongseon] Yes, I'm on it.

00:49:07.216 --> 00:49:11.637
Granny Mija has breast cancer?

00:49:21.355 --> 00:49:23.357
It's okay. I feel fine.

00:49:23.440 --> 00:49:24.441
[Mija grunts]

00:49:24.525 --> 00:49:26.944
Let's get you to a hospital, okay?

00:49:27.027 --> 00:49:30.281
Oh, I'm fine.

00:49:30.948 --> 00:49:33.951
Ma'am, migraines are a bad sign.

00:49:34.034 --> 00:49:36.370
We should get you to a hospital
for a checkup…

00:49:36.453 --> 00:49:38.622
I said you don't have to worry about me.

00:49:38.706 --> 00:49:40.082
I'll be fine.

00:49:40.165 --> 00:49:42.668
No, Grandma.

00:49:42.751 --> 00:49:44.920
Oh, my baby.

00:49:45.004 --> 00:49:46.964
-I'm fine, okay?
-No.

00:49:47.047 --> 00:49:49.049
-I'm fine.
-[crying]

00:49:49.717 --> 00:49:52.511
[Mija] Let's just go home, okay?

00:49:53.053 --> 00:49:54.430
Goodness.

00:49:55.598 --> 00:49:56.849
What's going on?

00:49:59.393 --> 00:50:00.644
Is it bad?

00:50:03.272 --> 00:50:05.482
I'm okay.

00:50:06.066 --> 00:50:10.237
Oh, my baby. Let's go home, okay?

00:50:10.321 --> 00:50:12.239
[groans, chuckles]

00:50:12.323 --> 00:50:15.200
I'm okay.

00:50:15.284 --> 00:50:17.036
[chuckles]

00:50:17.119 --> 00:50:18.787
I'm okay.

00:50:18.871 --> 00:50:20.539
My baby, I'm okay.

00:50:20.623 --> 00:50:22.958
-Grandma.
-My baby.

00:50:23.042 --> 00:50:24.126
[groans]

00:50:24.209 --> 00:50:27.254
I'm okay. Okay?

00:50:27.338 --> 00:50:29.965
Let's hurry up and go home, my baby.

00:50:30.049 --> 00:50:32.509
[Hari crying] No.

00:50:32.593 --> 00:50:37.222
[Mija] Goodness, I'm fine.

00:50:50.194 --> 00:50:52.112
How long have you known, Dr. Do?

00:50:54.865 --> 00:50:55.866
What?

00:50:55.949 --> 00:50:58.369
Shouldn't you share
crucial patient information?

00:51:00.663 --> 00:51:01.789
[Jiui sighs]

00:51:01.872 --> 00:51:05.209
I prescribed painkillers
for Ms. Oh Mija yesterday.

00:51:06.585 --> 00:51:09.004
Had I known, I would have given her
a proper prescription

00:51:10.673 --> 00:51:11.674
or done something.

00:51:15.928 --> 00:51:18.472
There's nothing you could have done
even if you knew.

00:51:19.056 --> 00:51:20.766
She's on Chavoxifen.

00:51:24.019 --> 00:51:25.854
She has stage four cancer.

00:51:27.356 --> 00:51:28.691
And the patient herself…

00:51:31.026 --> 00:51:34.238
didn't want people to find out about it.

00:51:36.156 --> 00:51:37.574
Not that it matters now.
STYLE
::cue()

00:51:44.957 --> 00:51:45.958
[Hari] Here.

00:51:46.834 --> 00:51:48.919
Let's have some of your favorite pasta.

00:51:49.503 --> 00:51:50.504
[Mija] Hmm.

00:51:54.133 --> 00:51:55.551
[Hari] Hmm.

00:52:03.475 --> 00:52:06.228
[slurping]

00:52:13.777 --> 00:52:14.778
Hari.

00:52:16.196 --> 00:52:18.782
It was just a one-time thing.

00:52:19.616 --> 00:52:21.869
I'm really okay.

00:52:23.120 --> 00:52:25.831
I know you're okay, Grandma.

00:52:31.336 --> 00:52:32.421
[sniffs]

00:52:33.130 --> 00:52:35.549
[♪ mournful music playing]

00:52:55.778 --> 00:52:57.821
[sniffing continues]

00:53:15.589 --> 00:53:17.257
[slurping]

00:53:18.550 --> 00:53:19.676
[sniffing continues]

00:53:31.104 --> 00:53:33.816
MS. YUK HARI

00:53:33.899 --> 00:53:35.734
[inhales deeply, sighs]

00:53:36.902 --> 00:53:38.612
[knocks on door]

00:53:38.695 --> 00:53:39.696
Yes?

00:53:51.875 --> 00:53:53.460
BOJUNGIKGITANG

00:53:53.544 --> 00:53:55.587
What's this?

00:53:56.255 --> 00:53:57.756
It's a herbal medicine.

00:53:58.507 --> 00:54:01.969
It works wonders for fatigue.

00:54:03.679 --> 00:54:05.722
Oh, thank you.

00:54:05.806 --> 00:54:08.600
Um, I'm sorry.

00:54:11.603 --> 00:54:13.313
I'm well aware

00:54:13.397 --> 00:54:16.525
how there was no way I could have detected
Deokhwa's acute epiglottitis.

00:54:17.818 --> 00:54:20.529
I know I just need to focus
on doing my job.

00:54:21.572 --> 00:54:23.282
But regardless, I'm really sorry.

00:54:25.158 --> 00:54:30.289
To you, to Ms. Hari,
and to Deokhwa as well.

00:54:36.253 --> 00:54:38.130
So please be sure to have it.

00:54:38.213 --> 00:54:40.883
It'll bring out the tiger in you.

00:54:41.884 --> 00:54:42.885
Oh.

00:54:45.262 --> 00:54:46.305
Get some rest.

00:54:53.937 --> 00:54:55.564
Bring out the tiger…

00:55:01.028 --> 00:55:02.654
[crickets chirping]

00:55:09.202 --> 00:55:11.121
Is this a little too corny?
STYLE
::cue()

00:55:22.883 --> 00:55:24.259
[Hari sniffs]

00:55:28.305 --> 00:55:29.348
[sighs]

00:55:39.399 --> 00:55:40.609
[sighs]

00:55:53.789 --> 00:55:55.123
[sighs]

00:55:57.542 --> 00:56:00.045
I'm sure there was more to the situation.

00:56:07.427 --> 00:56:09.721
[ship horn blows]

00:56:12.015 --> 00:56:14.393
[exhales]

00:56:17.312 --> 00:56:19.022
How's your grandma?

00:56:19.815 --> 00:56:21.316
-She's a lot better now.
-Hmm.

00:56:22.609 --> 00:56:24.903
The center will also
take special care of her,

00:56:24.986 --> 00:56:26.571
so don't worry too much. Okay?

00:56:26.655 --> 00:56:28.782
-[chuckles] Thank you.
-Mm-hmm.

00:56:45.090 --> 00:56:47.300
-Ms. Yuk, can we talk for a moment?
-Huh?

00:56:47.926 --> 00:56:49.386
Oh, sure.

00:57:23.253 --> 00:57:24.254
[sighs]

00:57:43.732 --> 00:57:45.192
[exhales]

00:57:46.693 --> 00:57:49.237
Could you close the door while you look?

00:57:49.321 --> 00:57:52.073
It's made of glass for a reason, you know.

00:57:52.157 --> 00:57:54.367
Of course. That's why it's made of glass.

00:57:55.702 --> 00:57:58.997
These. How much are these two?

00:57:59.080 --> 00:58:01.541
-Don't worry about it.
-Huh?

00:58:01.625 --> 00:58:04.377
I might run a shop, but I'm not heartless.

00:58:04.461 --> 00:58:05.754
You saved Deokhwa's life.

00:58:05.837 --> 00:58:07.631
There's no way I'm taking your money.

00:58:07.714 --> 00:58:09.466
No, you should still let me pay.

00:58:09.549 --> 00:58:10.550
No, it's fine.

00:58:10.634 --> 00:58:12.552
Just take it so I can bum a drink off you.

00:58:13.303 --> 00:58:15.138
Does that mean it's free for me too?

00:58:15.639 --> 00:58:16.973
Sure, why not.

00:58:17.057 --> 00:58:18.350
Score!

00:58:18.433 --> 00:58:20.060
Hold on a minute.

00:58:21.019 --> 00:58:23.271
Since you're here,
you should take this with you.

00:58:23.355 --> 00:58:24.481
Hold on, this…

00:58:25.106 --> 00:58:28.109
You cleaned out the whole shelf
when you came by yesterday,

00:58:28.193 --> 00:58:31.863
so I figured you loved 'em
and saved some more for you.

00:58:31.947 --> 00:58:34.032
-[chuckles]
-[Jiui] I see.

00:58:35.367 --> 00:58:37.118
I didn't know you liked gummies.

00:58:38.119 --> 00:58:40.163
I'll be going now. Thank you for this.

00:58:40.247 --> 00:58:41.873
-Yes.
-Right.

00:58:41.957 --> 00:58:42.958
Oh, my.

00:58:43.542 --> 00:58:44.626
[chuckles]

00:58:44.709 --> 00:58:46.461
-Granny, I'm off.
-Okay.

00:58:47.045 --> 00:58:50.340
♪ I ought to grab a beer with him ♪
STYLE
::cue()

00:58:54.094 --> 00:58:55.303
[chuckles]

00:58:55.387 --> 00:58:57.597
So you like these too, huh?

00:58:57.681 --> 00:58:58.849
[chuckles]

00:58:58.932 --> 00:59:00.308
It's not like that.

00:59:03.144 --> 00:59:04.771
Wait. Did you get these for me?

00:59:04.855 --> 00:59:06.565
Because they're shaped like burgers?

00:59:10.652 --> 00:59:11.653
Hmm.

00:59:12.279 --> 00:59:13.363
[chuckles]

00:59:15.156 --> 00:59:16.950
But why didn't you give them to me?

00:59:17.993 --> 00:59:19.744
I needed these yesterday.

00:59:21.454 --> 00:59:23.957
It's not that I didn't. I couldn't, okay?

00:59:24.583 --> 00:59:25.709
Why's that?

00:59:27.252 --> 00:59:28.336
Last night…

00:59:31.548 --> 00:59:34.301
I saw you with Dr. Chiyeon…

00:59:35.886 --> 00:59:37.304
in front of your house.

00:59:38.805 --> 00:59:41.933
It seemed like you two were having
an important conversation, so…

00:59:44.060 --> 00:59:46.605
Oh, there's something
I needed to tell you.

00:59:48.940 --> 00:59:50.942
[coughing]

00:59:51.026 --> 00:59:52.861
-[stammers] What is it?
-Huh?

00:59:52.944 --> 00:59:55.030
Oh, Dr. Chiyeon said
he's going to find a way

00:59:55.113 --> 00:59:57.991
for my grandma to get approved
for a clinical trial.

00:59:58.074 --> 00:59:59.367
Isn't that great?

00:59:59.451 --> 01:00:01.036
-Really?
-Yes.

01:00:01.912 --> 01:00:02.996
[sighs]

01:00:06.499 --> 01:00:08.418
And to think I thought you guys were…

01:00:08.501 --> 01:00:10.462
To think you thought we were, what?

01:00:14.633 --> 01:00:18.178
Come on! What did you think
was happening between us?

01:00:18.261 --> 01:00:20.847
Well, the two of you
seemed really close, so I…

01:00:23.475 --> 01:00:25.101
Were you jealous?

01:00:25.852 --> 01:00:26.853
[chuckles]

01:00:26.937 --> 01:00:29.105
No, I wasn't jealous or anything.

01:00:29.856 --> 01:00:31.483
Come on.

01:00:31.566 --> 01:00:33.360
I'm pretty sure you were jealous.

01:00:33.443 --> 01:00:38.031
-You were jealous, weren't you?
-Come on. Why would I be jealous?

01:00:38.114 --> 01:00:39.240
[Hari chuckles]

01:00:40.742 --> 01:00:43.453
I was just teasing you. [chuckles]

01:00:44.162 --> 01:00:46.081
It's not like I have any right
to be jealous.

01:00:48.917 --> 01:00:51.378
You said you would
never get your hooks into me.

01:00:55.048 --> 01:00:56.216
[Hari] Hmm.

01:00:59.469 --> 01:01:01.388
Remember what you said at the hospital?

01:01:02.555 --> 01:01:04.808
How it felt like
I was keeping my distance?

01:01:08.228 --> 01:01:11.272
Yes, you were right.

01:01:13.775 --> 01:01:15.318
I was keeping my distance from you.

01:01:18.279 --> 01:01:19.447
In case you caught on.

01:01:20.699 --> 01:01:23.326
[♪ romantic music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

01:02:17.172 --> 01:02:19.382
But why won't you get your hooks into me?

01:02:20.467 --> 01:02:23.595
If there's something you don't like
about me, tell me. I'll fix it.

01:02:48.661 --> 01:02:50.914
[♪ romantic song playing]

01:03:12.685 --> 01:03:13.895
I just got my hooks in.

01:03:18.358 --> 01:03:20.276
Where do we go from here?

01:03:33.373 --> 01:03:35.583
[waves crashing]

01:03:35.667 --> 01:03:37.585
[song continues]

01:04:13.997 --> 01:04:18.751
EVERYONE RUNS
WHEN THE PAIN GETS UNBEARABLE

01:04:18.835 --> 01:04:25.717
I ALSO RUN AWAY A LOT

01:04:30.096 --> 01:04:32.056
JUCHEON:
THERE'S A LOT OF TENSION IN THE AIR

01:04:32.140 --> 01:04:33.558
WHAT'S HAPPENING HERE?

01:04:34.225 --> 01:04:37.353
JEONGSEON:
I WAS ALREADY OVERWHELMED,

01:04:37.437 --> 01:04:41.024
AND DEALING WITH YOUR GLARE
MADE IT EVEN HARDER

01:04:45.612 --> 01:04:49.032
PERFECT LIGHTING IS
OUR WAY OF LOVING THE ACTORS

01:04:51.993 --> 01:04:53.536
[song ends]

01:04:53.620 --> 01:04:56.539
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

01:04:57.332 --> 01:04:58.875
[Hari] Today is officially day one for us.

01:04:58.958 --> 01:05:02.629
[Mija] Don't you know there are always
people watching on this tiny island?

01:05:02.712 --> 01:05:03.963
Ms. Yuk Hari.

01:05:04.047 --> 01:05:05.548
Pick a side and stick to it.

01:05:06.799 --> 01:05:09.093
I'm asking whose side you're on, okay?

01:05:09.177 --> 01:05:11.054
[Ms. Hwang] Are you fighting again?

01:05:11.137 --> 01:05:12.263
Now that you know, do it.

01:05:12.347 --> 01:05:13.848
No! I can't do it!

01:05:14.849 --> 01:05:15.975
Can we talk for a moment?

01:05:19.354 --> 01:05:20.438
[Hari] Dr. Do.

01:05:21.022 --> 01:05:23.566
It says you're to report
to Yeopoong-gun starting tomorrow.

01:05:25.944 --> 01:05:27.946
Translated by Yoon Hyuk Park